## 7. Test Fixture and Setup Guidelines

### 7.1 Fixture Design

- Use framework-provided fixture mechanisms for reusable setup and teardown
- Apply appropriate fixture scope: function, class, module, session
- Implement fixture finalization for guaranteed cleanup
- Parameterize fixtures for data-driven testing
- Document fixture purpose and dependencies

### 7.2 Test Data Seeding

- Create dedicated seed data functions per feature
- Support incremental seeding for large datasets
- Implement rollback mechanisms for failed seeding
- Version seed data with application changes
- Provide clear documentation for seed data structure

### 7.3 Environment State Management

- Verify environment state before test execution
- Implement health checks for dependent services
- Skip or fail fast if prerequisites are not met
- Support environment reset between test suites
- Log environment state for debugging failures

