## 9. Maintenance and Sustainability

### 9.1 Code Review Standards

- Require peer review for all test code changes
- Review for adherence to these guidelines
- Check for proper error handling and cleanup
- Verify test independence and isolation
- Ensure adequate step logging for debugging
- Confirm reports are readable to non-technical stakeholders

### 9.2 Technical Debt Management

- Track and prioritize test maintenance tasks
- Regularly review and update locators and selectors
- Refactor duplicated code into utilities
- Update dependencies on a scheduled basis
- Remove or update obsolete tests promptly

### 9.3 Documentation Requirements

- Maintain up-to-date README with setup instructions
- Document all configuration options with examples
- Keep pipeline variable documentation current
- Create onboarding guides for new team members
- Document known issues and workarounds

### 9.4 Metrics and Monitoring

- Track test execution time trends
- Monitor test pass/fail rates over time
- Identify and address flaky tests
- Measure test coverage by feature area
- Report on automation ROI periodically

