## 10. Quick Reference Checklist

### Before Selecting Framework

- [ ] Assess team's technical proficiency
- [ ] Identify who will author and maintain tests
- [ ] Determine stakeholder involvement in test specification
- [ ] Evaluate report readability requirements
- [ ] Consider all test types needed: UI, API, ETL
- [ ] Review existing team skills and preferences

### Before Writing Tests

- [ ] Understand the feature requirements thoroughly
- [ ] Identify test scenarios covering happy path and edge cases
- [ ] Determine test type: UI, API, ETL, or integration
- [ ] Check for existing utilities that can be reused
- [ ] Plan test data requirements

### While Writing Tests

- [ ] Follow naming conventions consistently
- [ ] Add hierarchical categorization: Epic → Feature → Story
- [ ] Wrap actions in reportable steps with Given/When/Then prefixes
- [ ] Use business language in step descriptions
- [ ] Externalize test data — no hardcoding
- [ ] Implement proper setup and teardown
- [ ] Add appropriate markers/tags for categorization
- [ ] Handle errors gracefully with meaningful messages

### Before Committing

- [ ] Run tests locally and verify they pass
- [ ] Ensure tests are independent and can run in any order
- [ ] Check that cleanup runs even on failure
- [ ] Verify no sensitive data is in the code
- [ ] Review generated report for readability by non-technical person
- [ ] Update documentation if adding new features

### Pipeline Integration

- [ ] Verify all required variables are documented
- [ ] Test pipeline with different variable combinations
- [ ] Confirm artifacts are generated correctly
- [ ] Check report accessibility and correctness
- [ ] Validate notifications are working
- [ ] Ensure reports are published and accessible

